## Project Structure

```
ebready/
├── ebkit/
│   ├── cli.py                  # CLI entry point (ebkit command)
│   ├── analyzer/
│   │   ├── scanner.py          # Heuristic repository scanner
│   │   └── ai_analyzer.py      # AI abstraction + Mock/OpenAI/Google
│   ├── models/
│   │   └── deployment_config.py # Strict Pydantic schema
│   ├── generator/
│   │   ├── renderer.py         # Jinja2 template renderer
│   │   └── templates/
│   │       ├── Dockerfile.j2
│   │       ├── Procfile.j2
│   │       ├── ebignore.j2
│   │       ├── env.example.j2
│   │       └── ebextensions/
│   │           └── config.yml.j2
│   └── commands/
│       └── init.py             # ebkit init implementation
├── tests/
│   └── test_ebkit.py
├── app/                        # EBReady FastAPI hello-world app
│   └── main.py
├── requirements.txt
└── pyproject.toml
```

---

## Current Limitations

- `ebkit init` generates files only — it does NOT deploy to AWS.
- The MockAIAnalyzer uses simple heuristics; real AI backends produce better results for complex projects.
- Django projects require manual review of the generated `start_command` (project name unknown at scan time).
- Multi-stage Dockerfile builds not yet supported.
- No support for monorepos with multiple services.

